est":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119141","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119141","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119141.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119141.patch","merged_at":"2026-05-26T15:14:29Z"},"body":"Fixes #118334 (maybe something else too).\r\n\r\nFigured out two fixes while playing around with touch using [Weylus](https://github.com/H-M-H/Weylus). Confusingly enough, they're related to the Godot mouse API.\r\n\r\nThis PR addresses the same rough issue (funky touch input) but I'm keeping two separate commits in case we need to revert either of them:\r\n\r\n * The most important fix is in the first commit, which ensures that the engine never gets weird mouse enter/exit event combinations. This was pretty tricky to do, as there were lots of edge cases to take into consideration.\r\n\r\n * The second is smaller but hopefully addresses some really annoying behavior. Previously it was possible to get the mouse position in the wrong coordinate space in certain circumstance. We now avoid that edge case altogether. I haven't tested is as much but I didn't notice anything weird for now.\r\n\r\nAs usual, you can find detailed explanations in the each commit's description.\r\n\r\nTested on KDE 6.5.4 and GNOME 49.2.2 (had trouble running Weylus on COSMIC).\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organ